.Dd October 26, 2023
.Dt FB 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm fb
.Nd framebuffer device driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/fb.h
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver provides a linear framebuffer interface for graphics devices.
It supports high-resolution graphics modes and hardware scrolling acceleration
when available (e.g., via the Bochs Graphics Adapter).
.Pp
The driver creates the
.Pa /dev/fb0
device node, which can be accessed via
.Xr mmap 2
to map the framebuffer memory into user space.
.Sh IOCTLS
The following
.Xr ioctl 2
calls are supported:
.Bl -tag -width FBIOGET_VSCREENINFO
.It Dv FBIOGET_VSCREENINFO
Get variable screen information, including resolution and color depth.
Returns a
.Vt struct fb_var_screeninfo .
.It Dv FBIOPUT_VIDEO_MODE
Set the video mode.
.El
.Sh HARDWARE SCROLLING
On supported hardware (like BGA), the driver allocates a virtual buffer
larger than the visible screen (typically 2x height). This allows for
accelerated console scrolling by adjusting the display start offset
rather than performing expensive memory copies.
.Sh FILES
.Pa /dev/fb0
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mmap 2 ,
.Xr vga 4
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
driver first appeared in the kernel. Hardware scrolling support was added later.
